This is an important point and the major lesson to be learned -
Your diety didn't get angry randomly.  It is something you did and
the game gave you a message telling you that when you did it.
Lesson - Remember what it is you did and don't do that again.
Alternate but even more important lesson - If you don't remember
the message then your lesson is to pay attention to each and
every message.  If the message isn't an expected one like "The
orc swings her scimitar" then READ it and *figure out what it
means*.  Nethack is a game played by humans and we go
through lots of character players.  We get to learn across their
deaths.

> >Is it on a timeout?
>
>   Nope.
>
> >How do I get happy here?
>
>   Sacrifice tough monsters.  The threshold varies depending on your
> character's god.  Chaotics have a tougher time than the other religious
> orientations.

Note the implication of this - Monsters below some level of
toughness (XL) will do nothing for you no matter how many you
sac.  So sac a meaner monster and note the effect.  If you
get a feeling of inadequacy don't bother with any monster that
mean or less until your god is mollified.

Sac has several levels when it comes to monster size.  Once
already reconciled even a newt has a chance of an artifact.
Until reconciled the bigger the better the chance of
reconciliation but even a newt is worth the effort.  With an
angry diety only the meanest monster will help at all.

> >This is annoying.

It's an opportunity - Do you already know what you did to
anger your diety?  If you do then there's one lesson to be
learned.  If you don't then there's a different lesson to be learned.



